# CODEOWNERS -- githerd-rules
#
# Introduced by Githerd init-120 S16 (plan-142, adr-069 D13). Scope is
# deliberately narrow: broadening CODEOWNERS to other paths is a repository
# governance decision, not a subject vocabulary one.
#
# HONEST CAVEAT ON ENFORCEMENT. CODEOWNERS enforces nothing on its own; it
# only bites when a branch-protection rule requires code-owner review on the
# protected branch. On a single-maintainer repository the code owner and the
# author are the same account, so the guardrail buys an audit trail and a
# deliberate second look, not independent review.

# The Subject Vocabulary Standard: the core scheme every adopter vendors, its
# schemas and its reference implementations. githerd_subject_experiment_promote
# produces all-scope patches against the core scheme that a person applies;
# nothing is adopted until a code owner merges the pull request.
